853	     * Resolve this owner's effective {@code membershipLevel}: the capped value stored on the owner
854	     * when present (the create-time level after the household ceiling has been applied, see
855	     * {@link #getMembershipLevel()}), otherwise the level recomputed from the owner's membership
856	     * points (see {@link #membershipLevel(int)} and
857	     * {@link #membershipPoints(Integer, String, Integer, LocalDate)}). This is the single source of
858	     * truth for how a stored level is read back, deferred to by both the create-time household-ceiling
859	     * computation and the read-side DTO mapping so they always agree.
860	     *
861	     * @return the stored capped level when present, otherwise the level derived from membership points
862	     */
863	    public int effectiveMembershipLevel() {
864	        if (this.membershipLevel != null) {
865	            return this.membershipLevel;
866	        }
867	        return membershipLevel(membershipPoints(this.namesakeCount, this.email,
868	            this.householdCount, this.registrationDate));
